# local env files
# `.env` stays IGNORED (re-confirmed 2026-07-31 after a brief plan to track it).
# It is not needed for a fresh clone: `EXPO_PUBLIC_API_MODE` is read in exactly
# ONE place (`app/_layout.tsx`, `=== 'mock'`), so an absent `.env` means "not
# mock" — the real API, which is the correct default for preview/production.
# Tracking it would only add a way to accidentally ship `mock` to users.
# NEVER put a real secret here either: `@expo/env` exports `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` ONLY,
# so a secret would silently fail to load *and* be inlined into every bundle.
.env
.env*.local
!.env.example
# Sentry's local-credentials file. It matches NEITHER `.env` (exact) NOR
# `.env*.local`, so without this line it would be tracked. The OTA flow
# deliberately does NOT use it — the token is pulled from `eas env` at publish
# time via `eas env:exec` (see `rules/ARCHITECTURE.md → Observability`), so no
# credential ever lands in the tree. Ignored so a stray local copy can't be
# committed by accident.
.env.sentry-build-plugin
sentry.properties

# Google Play service-account key used by `eas submit --platform android`
# (eas.json -> submit.production.android.serviceAccountKeyPath). It can publish
# releases to the Play Console, so it is a real credential: never commit it.
# Prefer a GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY file secret in `eas env` over a local path.
google-service-account.json
*-service-account*.json
play-store-credentials.json

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo

example

# generated native folders
/ios
/android

# Session state
.remember/
